\end{equation}
If  $F=(f^1,f^2,f^3,f^4, f^5, f^6)\in \mathcal{H}$ then the solution $U=(\phi,\Phi,\psi, \Psi,\theta,\Theta)\in\hbox{D}(\mathcal{B}_2)$ the resolvent equation $(i\lambda I- \mathcal{B}_2)U=F$ can be written in the form


\begin{eqnarray}
i\lambda \phi-\Phi &=& f^1\quad\rm{in}\quad D(A^\frac{1}{2}),\label{esp-10B}\\
